CONTRACTS={
'00a':'main() prints a greeting containing Hello, the actual sys.executable, and the 1200-hour budget. It must work repeatedly without hidden notebook variables.',
'01a':'calculate(a, operator, b) returns a finite numeric result for + - * /. temperature(value, source, target) uses C/F units. profit(buy,sell,shares) returns (sell-buy)*shares; bmi(mass_kg,height_m) is arithmetic only. main(read=input, write=print) accepts commands calc A OP B, temp VALUE C F, profit BUY SELL SHARES, quit. Catch expected input errors, print a message containing error, and continue. Unexpected programmer errors propagate. The test suite includes five valid cases for each of the four arithmetic/conversion functions.',
'01b':'ContactBook exposes add(email,name,phone=""), update(email, name=None, phone=None), search(query), delete(email), save(path), and classmethod load(path). Normalize email by strip/casefold, reject duplicates with ValueError and missing updates with KeyError. Search returns fresh record dictionaries with email/name/phone. Delete returns bool. analyze(text,limit=5) returns characters, words, unique_words, top_words as (word,count) pairs, and most_common (or None); use lowercase ASCII words and alphabetical ties.',
'01c':'load_expenses(path) returns records with date as datetime.date, category as text, and amount as Decimal. Header is date,category,amount. Bad rows raise ValueError containing the CSV line number. summarize(records) returns count, total, average, highest, by_category, by_month. Money is decimal text; month keys are YYYY-MM; mean/highest are None for no records. Use temporary paths supplied by the tests.',
'01d':'factorial(n) accepts only nonnegative integers. directory_bytes(path) recursively counts regular-file bytes and excludes symlinks. compare_search(n,repetitions) returns n, repetitions, linear_seconds, binary_seconds, and an assumption statement about sorting. ExpenseAnalyzer(repository).report() calls repository.read() and returns the expense summary contract from 01c. main(argv) is the CLI boundary and returns a nonzero exit code for expected file failures. Reuse your previous modules via imports; you need not put their implementations in one file.',
'02a':'Use Python lists for vectors and nested lists for matrices. add/dot require equal vector lengths. transpose requires a nonempty rectangular matrix; matmul requires matching inner dimensions. norm/distance/cosine return scalars; zero-vector cosine raises ValueError. rotate takes a two-entry vector and a counterclockwise angle in radians. Outputs are checked with floating-point tolerance where needed.',
'02b':'fit(xs,ys,steps=1000,lr=.02,penalty=0) returns (weight,bias,loss_history), initialized at zero. Each history entry is the objective BEFORE that update; update both parameters using their old values. objective(w,b,x,y,penalty) is mean squared error plus penalty*w*w. gradient_check returns the maximum absolute error between analytical and central-difference derivatives. A nonzero L2 penalty changes the optimum; a large rate is intentionally allowed so the divergence experiment is observable.',
'02c':'mean, variance(sample=True), standard_deviation(sample=True), covariance, correlation operate on numeric sequences. Sample covariance uses n-1. Reject insufficient or mismatched samples and undefined constant-vector correlation with ValueError. permutation_test(a,b,repeats,seed) tests the absolute mean difference with private seeded randomness and the (extreme+1)/(repeats+1) convention.',
'03a':'clean(frame) returns (valid_dataframe, quarantine_dataframe, rolling_series, report_dict), without changing the input frame. Input columns: date/category/amount. Quarantine adds source_row (header means first row is line 2) and reason including invalid_date, invalid_amount, blank_category, or exact_duplicate. Complete calendar gaps with zero recorded spending before a trailing three-day mean. Report input_rows/valid_rows/quarantined_rows and the exclusion policy.',
'03b':'queries() returns SQL strings keyed inner, left, having, cte, missing, union, window. Offline schema: answer_lab.customers(id,name), answer_lab.records(id,customer_id,category_id,cents). The test seeds A/B/C and sales 100+200 for A, 50 for B, none for C. The test file specifies result columns for each query. rollback_example(connection) begins a transaction, writes customer 9001 and a related record, then rolls both back. SQLite tests portable query semantics; PostgreSQL index plans and constraints are separate live checks.',
'03c':'create_app(location,keys,seed=False,limit_per_minute=60) returns a FastAPI app with the Stage 03 route contracts. keys maps a credential of at least 24 characters to a tenant. GET /records requires auth; POST /records creates integer cents/category and returns 201. /summary and /statistics return count/total_cents. Responses carry X-Request-ID. ingest(store,tenant,path) uses the supplied course Store repository, validates the whole CSV before writing, and is idempotent for identical input.',
'04a':'regression() returns validation metrics by model (mean/linear/tree/forest/boosting), selected (minimum validation MAE), and final_test metrics. Each metric dictionary has mae/rmse/r2. classification() returns validation_macro_f1 for majority/logistic/forest/boosting, selected, test classification report, confusion_matrix, classes, and individual errors. Tests validate report consistency; review the split/fitting code separately to establish no leakage.',
'04b':'novel_tickets() returns at least 20 unique id/text/label/provenance records with access/billing/technical labels. ticket_errors() adds predicted, correct, review_category. clustering(output) runs blobs/moons with kmeans/dbscan and returns comparisons (dataset/model/ari_external_diagnostic plus other measurements), PCA results, and writes clusters.png. Synthetic labels may diagnose results but should not be secretly used for selection.',
'05a':'loss_grad(x,y,params) returns (scalar_MSE, gradients). params=[W1,b1,W2,b2]; use tanh hidden activations, linear scalar outputs, and a batch mean loss. Return gradients in parameter order with matching shapes. Do not mutate weights while calculating gradients. The tests independently perturb ten coordinates and train on four XOR examples; plotting and optimizer comparison remain project evidence.',
'05b':'digits_comparison(output,epochs=8) returns experiments, selected, test_report, errors, split_seed, model_card. Each experiment records name/architecture/best_validation_loss/epochs/parameters/seconds/history; history has training/validation loss per epoch. Save best_weights.pt and validation.png in the existing output directory. The automatic test uses one CPU epoch and checks mechanics, not a high accuracy threshold.',
'06a':'probabilities(logits,temperature=1,top_k=None,top_p=1) returns a normalized NumPy vector with stable softmax and filtering. Invalid sampling parameters raise ValueError. entropy(p) uses natural logs and zero contribution for zero probabilities. causal_attention(q,k,v) accepts 2D arrays and returns (outputs,weights), with no weight above the causal diagonal.',
'06b':'CachedLM(vocab,blocks=2,width=24,context=128) is a torch.nn.Module. forward(ids,cache=None) returns (logits, updated_cache). IDs have shape batch/length. Cache is one (K,V) tensor pair per layer with shape batch/heads/length/head_dim. Preserve absolute position offsets when extending it; reject context overflow. Full and cached eval-mode logits must agree. Implement your own block internals; tests do not require a particular parameter naming scheme.',
'06c':'extract_revenue(text) supports exactly one statement of the form COMPANY revenue was $NUMBER million/billion under the fictional USD convention. Supported results include status=supported, company, revenue as exact decimal text, currency, quote, start/end offsets. Other/ambiguous statements return status=unknown. offline_smoke() performs an actual tiny random-model adapter backward/update step and reports finite loss/trainable_parameters; it is explicitly not a pretrained benchmark.',
'07a':'chunks(document,size,overlap) accepts id/text/source/tenant/public fields and returns chunks with id/document_id/text/start/end/sha256/parser_version plus scope. start/end are exact character offsets. bm25(query,documents) returns one score per document. rankings(query,documents,tenant) returns keyword/vector/hybrid/reranked lists of authorized document dictionaries. The offline vector path can be TF-IDF if explicitly labeled; learned embedding comparisons remain a separate experiment.',
'07b':'parse_document(path) extracts supported file text, excluding HTML script/style text. documents_from_paths(paths,tenant) returns id/text/source/tenant/public records; use content-versioned identities, public=False for uploaded files, and PDF page provenance. Empty extraction or unsupported formats raise ValueError. Offline tests cover Markdown/HTML/JSON; the PDF/model/vector-database integration remains explicit evidence.',
'08a':'ResearchWorkflow(store,tenant,max_calls=5,seconds=10) exposes execute(call) and run(calls). Calls have exactly tool/arguments. Allow search(query,k), financials(companies,years), divide(numerator,denominator). run returns status=complete/failed/budget_exhausted and observations with status/result/error. Reject caller tenant overrides, unknown tools, zero denominator, and nonfinite values. Trusted scope is supplied separately from arguments.',
'08b':'build() returns a LangGraph that interrupts for a proposal and resumes using approved/fingerprint. fingerprint(state) binds actor/proposal. ReviewStore(path) provides propose(run_id,actor,proposal,now=None,ttl=300) returning a fingerprint and resume(run_id,actor,fingerprint,approved,execute,now=None) returning status/result. Verify actor, exact fingerprint, expiry, and one-time status across reopened instances; unknown actor raises PermissionError and altered/expired/consumed proposals raise ValueError.',
'09a':'memory_budget() returns all 27 parameter-count (1B/7B/14B), precision (4/8/16), and context (2048/8192/32768) scenarios. Rows have parameters,bits,context,weight_gib,kv_gib,assumption. State the KV architecture and distinguish estimates from actual observed machine memory.',
'09b':'measure(operation,runs=30,concurrency=1) invokes a supplied callable returning text and optional tokens. Return observations (ok/seconds plus tokens/output_characters or error type), runs, concurrency, wall_seconds, failures, p50_seconds_all_attempts, p95_seconds_all_attempts, tokens_per_wall_second. Include failed attempts. Throughput is unknown (None) if successful token counts are unavailable. Reject nonpositive run/concurrency sizes.',
'10a':'run(output) actually exercises local HTTP failures and SQLite recovery, writes report.json and operations.html, and returns faults with case/status/expected/ok/seconds/request_id as applicable, simulated_model_timeout, sqlite_restore, passed, limits. Required cases include invalid_auth/malformed_body/oversized_prompt/missing_period/database_outage/corrupt_document. Tests inspect observed values, not just the passed flag. This local harness does not substitute for live service outages.',
'10b':'restore_copy(source,target) performs a real SQLite backup into a new path, verifies integrity, and returns (record_count,total_cents) for the records table. Reject an existing target with FileExistsError and preserve it byte-for-byte. This is the local recovery component; PostgreSQL, Compose, release, and deployment checks require their own evidence.',
'11a':'streaming_totals(rows=1000000,batch_size=10000) computes account=id%50 and cents=(id*17)%10000. Return rows/groups/total_cents/by_account/maximum_batch_size. by_account uses integer keys. Process incrementally rather than retaining all rows. Reject negative row count or nonpositive batch size.',
'11b':'Expose streaming_totals as in 11a and spark_comparison(rows,output). The latter runs real Spark at partitions 2/8/32, reconciles aggregates, compares salted totals, and performs a broadcast join. Return runs with partitions/seconds/total_cents, salted_totals_match, broadcast_join_rows; write plan-2.txt/plan-8.txt/plan-32.txt/broadcast-plan.txt. The Spark test is opt-in; an offline pass leaves it pending.',
'12a':'fixtures() returns >=20 uniquely named HTTP method/path/key/expected-status inputs. threat_model() returns concrete asset/entry/impact/control/residual rows. run(output) executes the fixtures and returns checks, permission_matrix, limits. Matrix rows contain tenant/resource/expected/observed/passed, with both allowed and denied controls. Inspect actual report traces; report-shape checks cannot prove complete attack coverage.',
'12b':'ScopedDocuments(store,keys) exposes get(key,id) and revoke(key); reauthorize each fetch and raise PermissionError for unauthorized/revoked access even after caching. endpoint_matrix(path) runs all ten business/health route-method combinations for alice/alex in A, bob/blair in B, plus anonymous. Return user/method/route/expected/observed/passed records. The app model is tenant-wide sharing, not per-user document ownership.',
'13a':'reference_cases() returns >=40 dev and >=20 holdout labels with unique id, question, company, year, field, expected, source_id, group, tenant, category, split, label_status. For the bundled numerical fixture, field is revenue/operating_margin/free_cash_flow. Groups may not overlap between dev and holdout. Labels must match source arithmetic. Broader failure/abstention cases and human review are separate evidence.',
'13b':'paired_interval(baseline,candidate,groups=None,repeats=2000,seed=42) returns delta,ci95,resampling_unit,groups. Resample paired differences or supplied source groups, keeping group members together. release_gate(report) returns False on empty cases or any incorrect/uncited/unauthorized case; cases contain correct/citation_correct/authorized booleans. Machine-readable CLI exit and real model comparisons remain end-to-end checks.',
'14a':'complete_ratios(rows) accepts dictionaries using the bundled financial CSV schema and returns sorted company/year ratio rows with decimal-text or None values. Preserve source_id, prior_source_id, and publication metadata. Use only consecutive same-company/currency/unit prior periods; first-year growth and average-balance ROE/ROA are unknown. Reject duplicate periods, unbalanced statements, and nonpositive shares. The tests include expected numeric values and incompatible-history cases.',
'14b':'publication_join(decisions,filings) uses company and strictly earlier publication time, with decision_time/published_at converted to compatible timestamps. strategy(frame,fee=.001) uses close prices, previous-period positive return as its signal, and a position known before each realized return. Return return/position_before_period/turnover/net_return/wealth columns, subtracting fee*turnover. This is a mechanics example, not evidence of investment performance.',
'15a':'create_app uses the Stage 03 interface and financial /compare endpoint. verify_rows(rows) checks exactly six unique company/year fixture results, correct revenue/operating_margin/free_cash_flow values, and matching source IDs. Reject altered values, invented sources, duplicate rows, and missing periods. Tenant denial and unknown-company behavior are exercised through real in-process HTTP requests.',
'15b':'growth(current,prior) is the sample unfamiliar feature from the defense guide. Input fields: company/year/revenue/currency/unit/source_id. Return status=answered, value as decimal fraction text, sources containing both prior/current IDs for comparable consecutive periods. Return status=unknown and value=None for missing prior, nonpositive base, or incompatible periods/units/company. Reject nonfinite amounts. The caller must authorize both records before invoking this arithmetic helper.',
}
